WEBVTT

00:07.600 --> 00:09.780
Along with my authority as a
 commander of Angelic Knights,

00:09.780 --> 00:12.150
I hereby relinquish my Sacred Sword.

00:14.530 --> 00:20.200
<i>When I was given the power of the Sacred Sword, 
I was proud to use it protect people.</i>

00:20.880 --> 00:24.380
<i>But at some point, I was simply 
doing the Church's bidding,</i>

00:24.380 --> 00:27.540
<i>unable to swing a sword 
of my own accord anymore.</i>

00:28.320 --> 00:30.210
<i>Which is why... this is for the best.</i>

00:31.510 --> 00:35.220
Chastille, please do not look so forlorn.

00:36.710 --> 00:41.100
Do I really seem completely unmoved 
from having to cast this judgment?

00:42.220 --> 00:47.410
It will take time, but eventually, 
your punishment will be rescinded.

00:47.410 --> 00:48.980
What do you mean, Your Excellency?

00:49.240 --> 00:52.740
The Sacred Swords choose their wielders.

00:52.960 --> 00:58.000
For one of the chosen to be punished
 like this would ordinarily be unthinkable.

01:00.020 --> 01:03.080
Which is why I ask you to remain patient.

01:03.080 --> 01:06.570
Old though I may be,
 I will find a way to resolve this.

01:06.570 --> 01:08.170
I am unworthy, sir.

01:08.810 --> 01:13.670
<i>There are still people in the Church 
who see the value in someone like me.</i>

01:13.900 --> 01:20.380
Be wary, though. The only protection 
I can offer you is of a political nature.

01:22.510 --> 01:25.270
A certain man is headed here.

01:25.710 --> 01:27.980
The most dreadful of the 
Sacred Sword wielders,

01:27.980 --> 01:30.020
Raphael Hyurandell.

01:31.440 --> 01:36.200
I'm sure you've heard the rumors of 
what a ruthless individual he is.

01:36.200 --> 01:38.860
I can only imagine why he is coming...

01:39.180 --> 01:42.500
<i>If the Dread Angelic Knight is 
arriving at a time like this...</i>

01:42.500 --> 01:47.710
<i>The only thing that comes to mind... is that 
he's coming to purge me as an apostate.</i>

01:50.830 --> 01:57.340
<i>I only became an Angelic Knight
to help as many people as I could reach.</i>

03:32.020 --> 03:37.020
<b>Episode 7: 
Even An Archdemon Should Know
 Better Than To Hit A Child</b>

03:43.950 --> 03:45.910
<i>The brand of an Archdemon...</i>

03:46.560 --> 03:50.460
<i>And the entities known as "demons" 
that exist somewhere in the world.</i>

03:51.840 --> 03:56.090
My king... by your command...

03:56.600 --> 03:59.880
<i>And the fact that one of those demons 
bowed down before that brand.</i>

04:00.330 --> 04:02.720
<i>I've been looking into it 
for the two weeks since.</i>

04:03.090 --> 04:08.030
<i>No clues have turned up among the 
materials I took from Marchosias' castle.</i>

04:11.270 --> 04:12.310
<i>It's Nephy...</i>

04:15.010 --> 04:18.770
<i>Is she trying to surprise me?</i>

04:15.850 --> 04:17.020
<b>Sneak</b>

04:16.860 --> 04:17.980
<b>Sneak</b>

04:17.820 --> 04:18.770
<b>Sneak</b>

04:19.270 --> 04:21.740
<i>Let's see what she does.</i>

04:23.600 --> 04:25.640
Guess who?

04:27.990 --> 04:30.120
Um... huh...

04:30.640 --> 04:32.190
What do I do now?

04:32.190 --> 04:34.460
I'm wondering the same thing myself!

04:34.790 --> 04:38.860
I thought I might be able 
to surprise you, Lord Zagan.

04:38.860 --> 04:41.060
To what end?

04:42.550 --> 04:44.550
I hadn't thought about that...

04:45.000 --> 04:49.230
But you've been looking exhausted 
from all of your research lately.

04:49.230 --> 04:50.350
So, I...

04:53.480 --> 04:55.820
<i>She was trying to cheer me up?</i>

04:55.820 --> 04:58.340
<i>If anything, the depths of her 
cuteness are what's surprising!</i>

04:58.340 --> 05:01.370
<i>What am I supposed to do 
when you're so adorable?!</i>

05:01.890 --> 05:04.360
So, did you need anything?

05:04.630 --> 05:05.920
Oh, right.

05:05.920 --> 05:08.320
Today's lunch is ready.

05:08.700 --> 05:14.400
The appetizer is a tomato and green vegetable
 salad with Caesar dressing and grated cheese,

05:14.400 --> 05:16.330
and a buttered rye roll on the side.

05:16.330 --> 05:18.960
The soup is a consomme with oatmeal.

05:18.960 --> 05:22.060
And for the main dish, sauteed lamb.

05:22.060 --> 05:24.630
<i>She's got more new recipes...</i>

05:24.630 --> 05:27.130
I'm curious, what's Caesar dressing?

05:27.430 --> 05:34.980
Well, from what Miss Manuela told me, 
a sorcerer named Caesar Kaldia came up with it.

05:34.980 --> 05:39.290
He's a rather unique individual whose studies 
focused on flavors instead of eternal life.

05:39.290 --> 05:42.400
He's said to have laid the 
foundation of modern cooking.

05:42.640 --> 05:45.510
That shop girl knows about cooking?

05:45.510 --> 05:47.420
Well, let's try it out then.

05:47.420 --> 05:48.160
Right!

05:55.620 --> 05:57.460
<b>Siiigh</b>

05:57.870 --> 06:01.520
I had no idea that food could taste so good.

06:01.520 --> 06:04.510
You say that every time, Lord Zagan.

06:04.510 --> 06:07.760
Also, for dessert today, 
I've prepared a pudding.

06:08.680 --> 06:09.720
Pudding?

06:09.720 --> 06:12.050
Miss Manuela taught me about it.

06:12.510 --> 06:15.240
It's a treat made with eggs and cream.

06:15.240 --> 06:17.730
She's really taken you under her wings.

06:17.730 --> 06:19.690
She hasn't done anything 
weird to you, has she?

06:19.990 --> 06:24.640
It's all right. She just had me try 
some embarrassing outfits on.

06:24.640 --> 06:27.070
I don't see how that's all right!

06:27.400 --> 06:30.940
Isn't it fine, since she's the only one 
who gets to see what it looks like?

06:30.940 --> 06:32.940
That's not really the point...

06:36.390 --> 06:39.580
How... do I eat this?

06:39.880 --> 06:42.490
Just use the spoon I set out.

06:47.550 --> 06:49.090
So sweet!

06:49.090 --> 06:49.880
Yes!

06:50.150 --> 06:55.510
<i>The outside world is so vast... I had no 
idea such a sweet, joyous flavor existed.</i>

07:02.190 --> 07:03.360
We've got a visitor.

07:03.360 --> 07:05.150
Should I greet them?

07:05.420 --> 07:07.680
No, it's fine. Leave it.

07:07.680 --> 07:08.650
But...

07:23.660 --> 07:25.380
This is an impatient one.

07:25.950 --> 07:29.820
<i>And they made it through all 
my traps. Not bad at all.</i>

07:37.280 --> 07:40.430
You're Zagan the Archdemon?

07:40.430 --> 07:44.890
Etiquette dictates giving your own 
name before demanding someone else's.

07:44.890 --> 07:47.860
That said, I think I saw you at the auction.

07:48.320 --> 07:50.120
Valefor the Apparition.

07:50.120 --> 07:52.360
One of the other Archdemon candidates.

07:52.360 --> 07:56.120
Archdemon Zagan! I will slay 
you and take your power—

07:56.120 --> 07:59.450
I'm in the middle of a meal.
 You'll need to wait.

08:03.830 --> 08:06.980
If you like, I can make some more later...

08:06.980 --> 08:10.760
That would be nice, but that's a separate 
issue from letting this batch go to waste.

08:10.760 --> 08:12.700
You're mocking me!

08:18.440 --> 08:21.230
<i>This arm... isn't from sorcery.</i>

08:25.690 --> 08:28.850
<i>Fool. I warned you!</i>

08:28.850 --> 08:33.420
You're going to get dirt on 
my food! Give it a rest!

08:36.810 --> 08:39.330
<i>I accidentally said what
 I was thinking out loud...</i>

08:40.980 --> 08:43.980
<i>Well, there's bound to be 
more incidents like this.</i>

08:43.980 --> 08:46.630
<i>I'll probably need to strengthen my barriers.</i>

08:50.960 --> 08:53.960
Leave him be, Nephy. It'll be a 
while before he's conscious...

08:53.960 --> 08:56.720
No, it's just... this girl...

08:56.720 --> 08:57.680
She's a girl?

08:59.200 --> 09:00.260
She's a child.

09:01.140 --> 09:05.890
<i>Did I just knock a little girl unconscious?!</i>

09:08.240 --> 09:13.320
C-C-Calm down, Nephy. 
I believe we have some cold medicine..

09:13.790 --> 09:17.450
You need to calm down, Lord Zagan! 
Cold medicine won't help with this!

09:17.740 --> 09:19.960
She's just unconscious.

09:19.960 --> 09:21.480
R-Right...

09:21.480 --> 09:22.960
She's not dead or anything.

09:22.960 --> 09:23.700
No.

09:26.320 --> 09:27.580
Good grief...

09:27.870 --> 09:30.090
This is one troublesome intruder.

09:32.210 --> 09:35.410
Lord Zagan, you really are kind.

09:38.610 --> 09:41.220
I never thought I was going 
to use this guest room,

09:41.600 --> 09:46.410
but it's a good thing I had it cleaned up
 in case one of your friends came by.

09:46.410 --> 09:47.520
It really is.

09:49.820 --> 09:51.420
Where am I?

09:55.800 --> 09:56.610
You!

09:57.680 --> 09:59.900
You owe Nephy some thanks.

09:59.900 --> 10:02.620
Without her, I would've twisted your 
head off your neck and thrown it out.

10:03.790 --> 10:07.080
<i>Not that I would ever do 
something like that around her.</i>

10:10.050 --> 10:11.040
Why?

10:11.040 --> 10:12.130
Why what?

10:12.400 --> 10:16.140
I came here to kill you.

10:16.140 --> 10:18.630
I'm your enemy. Why let me live?

10:19.090 --> 10:22.410
Like I said, Nephy saved you.

10:22.410 --> 10:25.390
So you get to live. It's that simple.

10:25.710 --> 10:28.640
Why did you attack me, anyway?

10:29.200 --> 10:31.140
I wanted power...

10:32.610 --> 10:34.780
Because I'm weak.

10:35.260 --> 10:39.150
I see. I do agree that power 
is necessary for survival.

10:39.480 --> 10:42.370
Why go after me, of all the 
possible targets, then?

10:42.700 --> 10:45.530
You're the newest Archdemon...

10:45.530 --> 10:49.270
And since you're known as the Sorcerer Slayer,

10:49.270 --> 10:51.630
I thought I could beat you
if I didn't use sorcery.

10:51.910 --> 10:57.190
It's true that I can't neutralize your 
racial abilities, since they're not sorcery.

10:57.190 --> 10:58.340
Her race?

10:58.730 --> 11:00.340
Durable scales...

11:00.580 --> 11:02.260
Photonic breath.

11:02.260 --> 11:04.040
You're a dragon, aren't you?

11:04.890 --> 11:07.510
I'm surprised to encounter a living one.

11:07.510 --> 11:10.200
It's said that dragons can 
live for hundreds, thousands,

11:10.200 --> 11:13.610
and in some cases, 
even tens of thousands of years.

11:14.770 --> 11:15.820
Because...

11:16.670 --> 11:19.200
<i>Something about this is off-putting.</i>

11:19.200 --> 11:23.450
<i>She's got no grand ambition or 
vendetta. This is more like...</i>

11:23.680 --> 11:24.870
<i>I know!</i>

11:25.110 --> 11:26.850
<i>That's what she reminds of!</i>

11:26.850 --> 11:30.660
<i>She's just like me when I got 
caught stealing food as a kid!</i>

11:30.960 --> 11:34.000
<i>I would go after easy-looking marks,</i>

11:31.290 --> 11:32.710
<b>I want some bread</b>

11:33.290 --> 11:34.000
<b>You little thief!</b>

11:34.000 --> 11:37.460
<i>and instead I ended up taking a beating, 
and almost broke down in tears.</i>

11:34.250 --> 11:35.880
<b>I want power</b>

11:37.810 --> 11:43.080
<i>Of course. Before being a 
sorcerer or a dragon, she's a kid.</i>

11:43.520 --> 11:45.720
<i>Which means there's only 
one appropriate response.</i>

11:47.040 --> 11:49.280
You challenged an Archdemon.

11:49.280 --> 11:51.450
That means you must be punished.

11:52.810 --> 11:53.650
Lord Zagan—

11:53.650 --> 11:54.690
I command you...

11:54.690 --> 11:57.860
To assist Nephy for a week!

12:00.150 --> 12:04.610
<i>While she's helping out, I can teach 
her what is and isn't allowed.</i>

12:04.950 --> 12:10.290
<i>Morality isn't my thing, but I can teach 
her how to behave, even as a villain.</i>

12:10.580 --> 12:14.290
<i>If she makes the same mistake 
after that, then it's not on me.</i>

12:16.590 --> 12:18.960
You're not going to eat me?

12:20.220 --> 12:23.150
<i>I know I look like a bad guy, 
but even for someone like me,</i>

12:23.150 --> 12:26.600
<i>being treated like a literal 
child-eater hurts...</i>

12:26.910 --> 12:31.140
Humans think that eating 
dragon flesh will make them stronger.

12:31.900 --> 12:33.270
Is that true?

12:33.620 --> 12:36.440
Bathe in dragon blood for immortality.

12:36.910 --> 12:39.810
Devour their flesh for infinite mana.

12:40.310 --> 12:43.280
Process their bones into 
elixirs that can cure any illness.

12:43.770 --> 12:46.870
There have been legends like 
that since ancient times.

12:47.180 --> 12:50.120
<i>I guess that's why she hid her identity.</i>

12:50.120 --> 12:51.520
But don't make me laugh.

12:52.370 --> 12:56.870
All I would get from devouring a
 brat like you is a nasty aftertaste.

12:57.670 --> 12:58.920
<b>Ugh...</b>

12:59.240 --> 13:01.630
<i>This is why I hate kids.</i>

13:02.000 --> 13:03.200
<i>Thinking back,</i>

13:03.200 --> 13:07.470
<i>what did the other older kids who 
grew up amongst the garbage do?</i>

13:18.250 --> 13:20.930
Nephy. Do we have any leftovers from lunch?

13:25.320 --> 13:27.340
What are you planning?

13:27.340 --> 13:30.770
Are you unfamiliar with 
the concept of charity?

13:30.770 --> 13:33.790
It's something that the 
strong offer the weak.

13:35.870 --> 13:41.150
For the record, I hate 
people who waste food.

13:41.150 --> 13:44.040
And when it's food made by Nephy...

13:44.690 --> 13:45.760
I kill them.

13:57.750 --> 13:59.310
It's so good...

13:59.310 --> 14:02.160
Obviously. Nephy made it.

14:02.160 --> 14:03.360
Thank you.

14:13.690 --> 14:15.200
I'm heading back to the library.

14:15.470 --> 14:17.960
Once you finish eating, 
help Nephy with what she needs.

14:17.960 --> 14:19.410
W-Wait!

14:19.960 --> 14:23.130
What if I were to attack this woman?

14:23.130 --> 14:25.090
Even if I didn't, I could escape...

14:25.480 --> 14:27.130
Suit yourself.

14:27.520 --> 14:33.640
I'm sure you realize what'll happen if you 
try to run, now that I know your secret.

14:35.150 --> 14:36.180
Besides...

14:36.180 --> 14:38.390
You've got the wrong idea.

14:38.390 --> 14:41.270
Nephy is much stronger than you.

14:43.020 --> 14:48.030
<b>An Archdemon's Dilemma:
How to Love Your Elf Bride</b>

14:49.190 --> 14:51.320
<i>I told her to suit herself, but...</i>

14:51.320 --> 14:54.580
<i>I hope things don't actually get dangerous.</i>

14:54.880 --> 14:58.300
Miss Valefor, could you 
take care of this laundry?

14:58.300 --> 14:59.970
I'll fold them later.

15:01.020 --> 15:04.240
Did you make that soup, Nephy?

15:04.240 --> 15:04.840
Yes.

15:05.870 --> 15:07.340
It was... good.

15:07.340 --> 15:09.290
I'm glad to hear it.

15:09.290 --> 15:13.300
You're also free to use anything 
in your room, Miss Valefor.

15:13.710 --> 15:16.950
You can call me... For.

15:19.090 --> 15:20.850
Okay, For.

15:20.850 --> 15:23.860
Are you afraid of Lord Zagan, For?

15:24.140 --> 15:29.860
Not his face. If his mouth were wider,
 I'd even say he was handsome.

15:29.860 --> 15:32.740
<b><i>Graaargh</i></b>

15:30.870 --> 15:32.740
I... see?

15:33.210 --> 15:35.490
<i>I guess that's a dragon's sense of beauty.</i>

15:35.490 --> 15:37.720
His power is scary.

15:37.720 --> 15:39.500
I didn't stand a chance.

15:39.860 --> 15:43.920
It's okay. Lord Zagan doesn't wield 
his power without a good reason.

15:44.180 --> 15:45.460
<i>Is that really true?</i>

15:45.460 --> 15:49.010
<i>I've vaporized my fair share 
of bandits and sorcerers.</i>

15:49.560 --> 15:53.660
Right. He didn't show even 
a glimpse of his true power.

15:53.660 --> 15:54.760
Such a strange human.

15:55.030 --> 15:57.390
He's a very mysterious person.

16:00.280 --> 16:03.180
What are you going to do after this, For?

16:03.650 --> 16:04.770
I don't know.

16:05.340 --> 16:08.900
I'm too weak to target one 
of the other Archdemons.

16:09.120 --> 16:12.000
You must really need power then?

16:12.000 --> 16:12.610
Yes.

16:13.230 --> 16:17.580
<i>I thought dragons would be some of 
the most patient creatures to exist.</i>

16:18.010 --> 16:22.960
<i>What's a dragon child doing in a human 
settlement acting like a sorcerer, anyway?</i>

16:23.360 --> 16:26.920
Nephy, why do you obey that man?

16:27.220 --> 16:30.490
I came here when Lord Zagan bought me.

16:30.490 --> 16:35.930
But he treats me like a person, not a slave.

16:36.430 --> 16:39.430
Which is why... this is where I want to be.

16:41.440 --> 16:43.890
Do you have a place like that, For?

16:45.280 --> 16:46.060
No.

16:55.570 --> 16:57.910
<i>This is why I hate kids.</i>

16:59.820 --> 17:01.410
<i>In the following days,</i>

17:01.800 --> 17:07.730
<i>Valefor slowly began to relax and 
started working without complaints.</i>

17:10.330 --> 17:12.350
<i>No clues.</i>

17:12.350 --> 17:14.700
<i>I'll need to head back 
to Marchosias' lair...</i>

17:14.700 --> 17:16.720
<i>His Archdemon castle and 
take another look around.</i>

17:17.230 --> 17:19.520
<i>I have a hard time believing
 that a millennia-old Archdemon</i>

17:19.520 --> 17:22.670
<i>would have no interest at all in true demons.</i>

17:22.670 --> 17:25.190
<i>In that case, could he 
have hidden what he learned?</i>

17:25.590 --> 17:28.540
<i>The input of a sorcerer with a 
different perspective would help.</i>

17:29.840 --> 17:31.600
Dinner's ready.

17:31.600 --> 17:33.650
I see. Be right there.

17:36.370 --> 17:37.360
You...

17:37.600 --> 17:41.930
Don't think I might attack 
you with your back turned?

17:42.700 --> 17:47.060
If you let me live, I swear 
I'll kill you! I guarantee it!

17:47.060 --> 17:49.710
Until I see you dead, I'll never give up!

17:51.780 --> 17:55.330
Someone said something 
very similar to me recently.

17:55.330 --> 17:58.380
I told him to bring it on
 whenever he wanted to.

17:59.370 --> 18:01.860
Which is why you get the same answer.

18:02.370 --> 18:04.340
I'm ready whenever you are.

18:04.340 --> 18:08.230
And when you lose, you'll end up
 working for me even longer.

18:12.800 --> 18:14.570
Do you like it, For?

18:18.730 --> 18:19.570
Zagan.

18:20.740 --> 18:24.620
I'm... sorry I interrupted your meal before.

18:26.040 --> 18:29.340
You were eating Nephy's cooking... 
and I got in the way.

18:29.760 --> 18:31.420
It's natural you got angry.

18:32.840 --> 18:34.300
As long as you understand!

18:36.360 --> 18:38.340
<i>I think she'll be fine now.</i>

18:38.960 --> 18:39.760
Nephy.

18:39.760 --> 18:40.680
Yes?

18:40.680 --> 18:44.430
I'm thinking of taking her to 
investigate the Archdemon's castle.

18:45.600 --> 18:50.600
Are you crazy?! That'd be like sharing the
 former Archdemon's knowledge with me!

18:52.360 --> 18:54.130
Just like earlier!

18:54.130 --> 18:57.290
You let me into your library, 
where your vital secrets are kept!

18:57.290 --> 19:00.180
Didn't it occur to you I might steal them?!

19:00.180 --> 19:02.310
I don't really care. Go ahead.

19:02.840 --> 19:06.240
I consider techniques and knowledge 
things that are meant to be stolen.

19:06.720 --> 19:11.980
I killed and stole the knowledge of 
this castle's original owner, anyway.

19:11.980 --> 19:13.480
I don't understand you.

19:13.920 --> 19:17.460
You could force me to obey 
you. So why don't you?

19:17.460 --> 19:20.470
<i>Because it'd make Nephy sad!</i>

19:20.800 --> 19:24.850
It doesn't matter how long-lived you are as a
 dragon or how skilled of a sorcerer you are.

19:24.850 --> 19:27.000
In here, you're just a kid.

19:27.970 --> 19:31.640
And kids should behave like kids, which 
includes acting out when they feel like it.

19:32.070 --> 19:35.200
There's no one here that'll 
hold that against you.

19:37.570 --> 19:40.610
<i>Wait, was that me? Did I make her cry?</i>

19:40.610 --> 19:41.740
A kid...

19:43.780 --> 19:44.160
<b>Floof</b>

19:43.870 --> 19:45.580
S-Stop crying!

19:44.410 --> 19:44.780
<b>Floof</b>

19:45.030 --> 19:45.410
<b>Floof</b>

19:45.280 --> 19:45.580
<b>Floof</b>

19:45.780 --> 19:46.660
Floof

19:45.860 --> 19:47.680
For now, just eat!

19:46.530 --> 19:47.490
Floof

19:47.290 --> 19:48.200
Floof

19:47.680 --> 19:51.280
Nephy's cooking will dry 
those tears right up!

19:48.040 --> 19:48.910
Floof

19:48.750 --> 19:49.750
Floof

19:49.540 --> 19:50.540
Floof

19:50.290 --> 19:51.160
Floof

19:51.210 --> 19:52.000
Floof

19:51.280 --> 19:53.250
I'm not... crying.

19:51.790 --> 19:52.750
Floof

19:52.540 --> 19:53.040
Floof

19:53.730 --> 19:59.260
Granted, obeying an Archdemon 
would have its upsides for you.

19:59.610 --> 20:05.010
Dragon or not, someone would have to be a 
fool to risk upsetting me by going after you, kid.

20:06.320 --> 20:07.430
Okay.

20:08.180 --> 20:10.600
But... I'm not "kid."

20:12.640 --> 20:15.650
You can call me For, too, Zagan.

20:20.440 --> 20:24.860
Unbelievable... falling asleep 
right after eating.

20:25.250 --> 20:27.490
I guess kids will be kids, 
even if they're dragons.

20:27.490 --> 20:32.460
I think after you demonstrated you're 
not an enemy, she relaxed, Lord Zagan.

20:32.900 --> 20:36.580
It was the same way for me 
when I first got here.

20:36.840 --> 20:38.850
W-Well, you know how it is.

20:38.850 --> 20:42.300
You belong to me! So of course
 I'm going to take good care of you.

20:42.580 --> 20:45.070
Yes. Thank you.

20:45.070 --> 20:47.640
<i>I treated her like an object again!</i>

21:00.630 --> 21:02.280
Father...

21:03.930 --> 21:06.070
<i>Is she dreaming about her parents?</i>

21:09.300 --> 21:10.080
What is it?

21:10.440 --> 21:13.580
It's like... we have a child now.

21:15.890 --> 21:16.580
Ch...

21:16.840 --> 21:19.820
Ch-Ch-Child?!

21:20.550 --> 21:21.840
I-I didn't mean it like that!

21:21.840 --> 21:24.960
It's just, you seem to be taking an 
interest in her well-being, so, well...

21:24.960 --> 21:28.570
Oh, right, I-I understand! 
I get it. Don't worry!

21:27.800 --> 21:29.300
<b>Phew</b>

21:35.940 --> 21:37.930
<i>A child, a family...</i>

21:38.490 --> 21:43.320
<i>It might be absurd for an Archdemon like me to 
yearn for a normal idea of happiness, and yet...</i>

23:30.050 --> 23:35.050
<b>Next time: 
I Found a Dragon and
I Guess She's My Daughter Now</b>
